"""Task TH2: the eight picked themes (A B C D E G H J) reworked, two versions each, as drawn by hand BEFORE the readability fit.

check.py fits text and status colours (lightness only), tunes the track colours for colour vision and measures everything.
A0 is today's app, locked (the baseline of docs/research-themes.md). E2 and J2 carry a second mode (`pair`).

Besides colours a theme may only set these style tokens (no decoration, the user's rule):
  caps      section labels in capitals with tracking (drafting lettering, console labels)
  fNum      numerals and read-outs: 'mono' (JetBrains Mono, today), 'plex' (IBM Plex Mono), 'ui' (Inter, tabular)
  fTitle    panel, device and dialog titles: 'ui' (Inter), 'serif' (Source Serif 4), 'serifItalic'
  dash      minor grid lines and secondary hairlines dashed (1) or solid (0)
  edgeW     clip outline width in px
  clipHead  opacity of the clip's title band
  gridMinor strength of the sixteenth and lane-quarter lines relative to today (graph paper)
"""
import colorsys

def hsl(h, s, l):
    r, g, b = colorsys.hls_to_rgb(h / 360, max(0, min(100, l)) / 100, s / 100)
    return '#%02X%02X%02X' % (round(r * 255), round(g * 255), round(b * 255))

_H, _S, _b = 215, round(.25 * 45), 12
_L = lambda v: hsl(_H, _S, v)
TODAY_PAL = ['#4c8dff', '#3ecf8e', '#f5c84c', '#ff6b6b', '#ff9a3c', '#b583ff', '#4cc9f0', '#ff7ac8']
